r.lean#L120-L131","doc":"**`KummerSurfaceData` with both degrees zero**, whenever every admissible\ncover of `X` has a member equal to the whole space. A consistency check on the\nhypothesis class, not a surface statement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.eq_cechClass_one_of_forall_dominant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.eq_cechClass_one_of_forall_dominant","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechDominantCover.lean#L95-L108","doc":"**`Ȟ²` is a point when every admissible cover has a dominant member.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.Cover.refinesDominant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.Cover.refinesDominant","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechDominantCover.lean#L88-L93","doc":"Any cover refines a cover with a member receiving a map from `X`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.cechClass_eq_one_of_dominant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.cechClass_eq_one_of_dominant","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechDominantCover.lean#L80-L86","doc":"In the colimit `Ȟ²`, a cocycle on an admissible cover with a member `𝒰.obj o`\nreceiving a map from `X` has trivial class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.TwoCocycle.rel_one_of_dominant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.TwoCocycle.rel_one_of_dominant","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechDominantCover.lean#L55-L72","doc":"**A cocycle on a family with a dominant member is a coboundary.** In a thin\ncategory, if every `U i` maps to `U o`, then `c` is cohomologous to the trivial\ncocycle, via `α_ij := c_ijo`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}